I need the ground truth for: posiztion, orientation (Euler angle) and linear velocity. Maybe also the angular velocity of the body.



param.has_mocap: to set the starting point. Doesn't seem to change 
param.mipo_use_foot_ang_contact_model:  Better results when it's on.
param.mipo_use_md_test_flag: PPProblem. This doesn't work on 1
param.data_start_idx: its better to start from a higher value
Initial Covariance: very small is better

proc_n_pos_xy and z: for xy doesn't seem to be important; for z the best value is around 10-5 and changes only the height
proc_n_vel_xy and z: a small value is better. xy seems to be more important
proc_n_acc: better to have xy much then z.  
proc_n_ang: must use a low value otherwhys i get a lot of turbines in the graph. lower then 10-8
proc_n_om: a good value is low but not too much (around 1e-5)
proc_n_foot_pos: not influent
proc_n_foot_vel: very important. z must be a value higher then e-4. (good e-2) and after that it doesn't change. While x and y increasing them the upper path rotates clockwise

Biases:
The attendable value are between 10-7 and 10-6 for the gyro. 10-6 and 10-5 for the accelerometer. For this value the biases are very high. Changing th value also the position grap can change significantly.


The ctrl_n_foot_acc are not influent
meas_om_body: if I use very small value nothing changes. The z component is not influent. The xy give changes for values of 0.001 and higher
meas_acc_body: seems that are not much influent . It gives a better results for values close to 0.1/0.01
n_foot:height: this value should be equal or lower then 0.001. The smaller it is the higher are the oscillation of the height but the offset with the ground truth is smaller.

